1. The terminal event carries the provider's stop reason as
   metadata.providerStopReason (null when the stream ended without one), so the
   service decides every stop reason from the SDK's own union
   (apps/api/src/lib/chat/provider-stop-reasons.ts) instead of reading an
   unhandled one as "stop". Remove when upstream exposes the raw reason.
2. The max_tokens RUN_ERROR carries the message's usage, which it dropped.
   Upstream PR to be opened; remove when released.

